<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04UQ">Example <span data-tag="04UQ">10.2.1.28</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be the $1$-dimensional simplicial set associated to the directed graph depicted in the diagram </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ A \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  X \\ Y &amp;  B, \ar [l] \ar [u] } \]
</div>
<p> and let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{0}_{/X} \subseteq \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{/X}$ be the sieve spanned by the objects $A$ and $B$. Then $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{0}_{/X}$ is dense when regarded as a full category of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{/X}$ (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="03VD" href="/tag/03VD">8.4.1.5</a>), but not when regarded as a sieve on $X$ (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="04UN" href="/tag/04UN">10.2.1.26</a>). </p>
</article>
